<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45165" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Spūrinna</span></b> , ae, m.
		Etruscan, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the surname of several Romans.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The haruspex who warned Cœsar to beware of
				the Ides of March</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Div.
				1, 52, 119</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 9, 24, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Caes. 81</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 1, 6, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 11, 2</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Vestricius Spurinna,
				<i>a lyric poet</i>, <i>the leader of
				the Othonian party</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 2, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 18</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">2, 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 2, 7, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 1, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
